<goal merged-clauses>

G.3  EXAMPLE BANKS

G.3a  RENDER

      Entries are rendered vertically, unindexed, in fixed
      alphabetical order. Each entry sits one abstraction level above
      the expected answer. The own-words line is primary; examples
      attach to it. Skip is stated in the round header, not as a peer
      entry.

G.3b  SELECTION OF A BANK ENTRY

      A reply that identifies one or more bank entries is an
      affirmative act and populates the slot directly, verbatim and
      unannotated. No confirmation step, no narrowing step.

      Three forms count as identification:

        verbatim    the entry text, exactly or near-exactly
        positional  "the third one", "the last one", counted against
                    the rendered order, which is fixed and
                    alphabetical
        referential the entry named unambiguously in other words

      Multiple entries identified → all populate, joined as given.

      Under-resolution is accepted. A bank entry is a valid answer at
      the level Goal operates. Granularity beyond this belongs to
      later stages, not to additional questions here.

      LIMITS

      Silence, "skip", or no reply does not identify an entry and
      never populates. → open:.

      A referential reply that maps to more than one entry, or to
      none, is not identification. Ask once which entry was meant.
      This clarifies the reply; it does not refine the answer, and it
      is the only additional question this clause permits.

      Anything else is an own-words answer and populates as given.

§6  OUT OF SCOPE

  · selectable option sets (indexed render; presentation only —
    selection of an unindexed entry is valid, G.3b)

§7  ECHO CONTROL

  Structural properties that hold echo rate down:

  · bank entries never indexed
  · entries generic enough that selection under-resolves rather
    than misresolves
  · own-words line primary
  · [N/A] capped at twelve words

§D.9a  NO NEW NOUN

      (see G.3b — an example becomes a value only by user
      selection, never by system inference)

HANDOFF DISPOSITIONS

  ordinal reply          → populate (G.3b)

</goal>

